  "step_2": "The individual reports having chosen Lottery A because they preferred having a 1% higher chance of winning over gaining an additional 100 Euros. This indicates that the individual considered both the difference in outcomes (100 Euros) and the difference in probabilities (1% higher chance in A). The individual explicitly downplays the monetary difference in favor of the slightly higher probability of winning. Their justification centers on preferring a higher chance of a favorable outcome (winning something rather than nothing) over a marginally better outcome, which reflects a deliberate trade-off between outcome size and probability.",
